= Entropy — Technical =

== Shannon entropy ==
<pre>
H(X) = -Σ_x p(x) log_b p(x)
</pre>

For base 2, H is measured in bits.

== Gibbs entropy ==
<pre>
S = -k_B Σ_i p_i ln p_i
</pre>

For a microcanonical ensemble with W equiprobable microstates:

<pre>
S = k_B ln W
</pre>

== Formal similarity and scope ==
Shannon and Gibbs forms differ by units/constants and, more importantly, by the objects being modeled.

The probabilistic mathematics is shared; the physical interpretation requires a physical ensemble and thermodynamic context.

